FA.</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(d)<br />\n<em>L</em><sub>1</sub> : Finite language, regular.<br />\n<em>L</em><sub>2</sub> : Infinite language but regular.<br />\nHence both accepted by DFA and both are disjoint language, so nothing is common in intersection.</p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":3,"type":"MSQ","correct":"C,D","right":1,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Given the context free grammar below:</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/c14f5f97d64616c954365c8e88a712fe482604bf.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div>Which of the following regular expression represents the language generated by this grammar?</div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/03680e5858a3fa6666761a1598e24e160a3ca340.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/da499fa319750ed3ca975c01cd434cc68f273e36.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/c31dc667cc686a1adec039a8946ae77ff0aab640.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <img src=\"/media/e7149579fbf7bf8ed69536561ac062ba8c7b28d2.png\" align=\"absmiddle\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(c, d)</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/f20fbd40198e86e24cd9868a281a7d5641ed3ca5.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":4,"type":"MSQ","correct":"C,A,B,D","right":1,"wrong":0.33,"qtext":"<p>Which of the following, represents language accepted by finite automata.<br />\n“All string over {<em>a</em>, <em>b</em>} where every ‘<em>a</em>’ is immediately followed by atleast one <em>b</em>”.</p>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> (<em>ab</em> + <em>b</em>*)* <em>ab</em></div>","isCorrect":true},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> (<em>a</em> + <em>b</em>)* (<em>ab</em>)* (<em>a</em>* + <em>b</em>*)</div>","isCorrect":tru