chnical"},{"qnum":7,"type":"MCQ","correct":"D","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Consider the following languages:</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/0a6e6faa4d8f4c85df93d87e8d3d744dd075b0cd.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>","options":[{"letter":"A","text":"<div> <em>L</em><sub>1</sub> is non-regular, having equal 0’s and 1’s.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"B","text":"<div> <em>L</em><sub>3</sub> is regular and <em>L</em><sub>2</sub> is non-regular but DCFL.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"C","text":"<div> <em>L</em><sub>2</sub> is CFL and <em>L</em><sub>3</sub> is regular, <em>L</em><sub>2</sub> ⊆ <em>L</em><sub>3</sub>.</div>","isCorrect":false},{"letter":"D","text":"<div> <em>L</em><sub>2</sub> and <em>L</em><sub>3</sub> have same number of the states in the minimal DFA.</div>","isCorrect":true}],"nat":{"low":"","high":""},"solution":"<p>(d)<br />\n<em>L</em><sub>1</sub> is empty string, as having (0 or 1) as an option for string.<br />\n<em>L</em><sub>2</sub> is regular language, having string start and end with same symbol that of <em>L</em><sub>3</sub>.<br />\nSo <em>L</em><sub>3</sub> and L2 both are same language.</p>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":8,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Consider the following DFA:</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/b5068b6b7a4c684c40cba5100eab7e9fd7a63a3d.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div>Number of states in minimal DFA is ________?</div></div>\n<div><span>NAT</span>","options":[],"nat":{"low":"2","high":"2"},"solution":"<p>2</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/642a43ab8533c926ad9fd4e9471b4f49cdee5690.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div> </div>\n<div> </div>","subject":"Technical"},{"qnum":9,"type":"NAT","correct":"","right":2,"wrong":0,"qtext":"<p>Consider the following statements for language:</p>\n<div> </div>\n<div><img src=\"/media/555d6a26b1befc3ae1871dda5237b63f4616deba.png\" loading=\"lazy\" /></div>\n<div>How many statements are true?</div></div>\n<div><span>NA